WEBVTT

00:00:00.930 --> 00:00:06.100
<b><i>Chihayafuru 3</i></b>

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:07.930
<b><i>Chihayafuru 3</i></b>

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:12.990
The Golden Pavilion.

00:01:12.990 --> 00:01:15.300
Its official name is Rokuonji.

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:18.810
It's most famous for its reliquary 
shrine built by Ashikaga Yoshimitsu,

00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:20.980
and is a World Heritage Site.

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:21.940
It's gold...

00:01:21.940 --> 00:01:22.650
It's gold...

00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:24.070
I didn't know it was <i>that</i> gold.

00:01:24.070 --> 00:01:25.110
So gold.

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:27.740
I'm getting serious Sukhavati vibes...

00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:29.470
Chi-chan, let's take a picture together!

00:01:31.850 --> 00:01:32.970
Chi-chan?

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:35.180
<i>I thought about it all night,</i>

00:01:35.180 --> 00:01:37.580
<i>and only one answer came to me.</i>

00:01:37.580 --> 00:01:38.630
Chi-chan?

00:01:39.550 --> 00:01:43.150
This is his only chance to get 
as far as he can with karuta.

00:01:43.150 --> 00:01:45.440
<i>I had no idea, Taichi.</i>

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:49.940
<i>I never knew you were serious 
about becoming the Master.</i>

00:01:51.250 --> 00:01:54.000
<b>Favorite Cushion</b>

00:01:52.120 --> 00:01:53.990
<i>I never realized...</i>

00:01:55.000 --> 00:02:01.020
<i>Eyelashes was so serious about becoming
 the Master that he'd skip his class trip.</i>

00:02:02.380 --> 00:02:05.200
Dr. Harada, please stop swinging so hard!

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:06.770
You're making taxis stop!

00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:08.140
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

00:02:09.540 --> 00:02:12.380
<i>He's just like me!</i>

00:02:12.770 --> 00:02:17.700
Verse 8

00:02:12.770 --> 00:02:17.700
As 
friends
 and 
strangers

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:20.520
Dr. Harada's going for it again this year?

00:02:20.980 --> 00:02:23.020
<i>He's crazy.</i>

00:02:23.020 --> 00:02:25.650
<i>Why is a 57-year-old man 
so gung-ho about this?</i>

00:02:34.170 --> 00:02:37.670
Master/Queen 
East Japan Qualifiers

00:02:34.170 --> 00:02:37.670
Otsuka Karuta
 Memorial Hall

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:48.060
<b>Aim for Master</b>

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:48.060
<b>Arashi</b>

00:02:38.910 --> 00:02:41.730
Aw, you're embarrassing me, Mayu-tan.

00:02:41.730 --> 00:02:44.620
I know I've risen up the ranks
 faster than anyone else recently,

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:46.190
but it's too soon for me to be Master!

00:02:46.190 --> 00:02:48.060
That's not true at all, Akkun!

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:52.290
<i>All that separated victory from defeat in 
the Yoshino Tournament was that fault early on!</i>

00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:54.060
Skreeeee

00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:54.650
<i>My skill surpasses his!</i>

00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:58.780
Unnnngh

00:02:54.650 --> 00:02:57.030
<i>All that separated victory from 
defeat was that fault early on!</i>

00:02:57.030 --> 00:02:59.260
<i>My skill surpasses his!</i>

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:04.700
<i>Damn it! I was supposed to catch up to
Mashima in Class A by these qualifiers!</i>

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:04.700
Krrrrgh

00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:11.030
Excuse me.

00:03:12.050 --> 00:03:15.950
I applied to enter this tournament, 
but I'd like to withdraw.

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:16.460
Whaaaat?!

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:19.250
Sudo-san, what are you saying?!

00:03:19.250 --> 00:03:20.370
Just what you heard.

00:03:20.370 --> 00:03:22.080
You can't be serious about withdrawing!

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:28.340
Whichever one of us loses first has to skip
the Master qualifiers in two weeks.

00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:29.670
No!

00:03:29.670 --> 00:03:32.900
If you don't participate, what'll happen 
to the Hokuo Society's morale?!

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:35.000
It'll plummet in a free fall!

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:37.360
Shut up. Just do your best by yourselves.

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:39.850
We can't do our best if you're not there!

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:41.860
You don't have to withdraw, Sudo-san.

00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:43.860
Take part.

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:43.780
Excuse me?

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:48.250
Sudo-kun... Sudo-kun...

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:48.250
Don't be dumb! I may break promises, 
but I won't owe anyone over a bet!

00:03:48.470 --> 00:03:50.100
It's not about that...

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:52.140
I refuse! I absolutely refuse!

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:54.050
I will never owe anyone anything!

00:03:54.050 --> 00:03:55.550
Ugh, you're so annoying!

00:03:55.550 --> 00:03:58.540
Then just yield to me if we're matched up.

00:04:03.330 --> 00:04:06.730
I didn't bring my shirt, though.

00:04:06.730 --> 00:04:08.010
You can use mine!

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:08.740
No, mine!

00:04:08.740 --> 00:04:09.230
Use mine!

00:04:09.990 --> 00:04:11.510
<i>Mashima...</i>

00:04:11.510 --> 00:04:14.010
<i>He just picked up a hell of a joker.</i>

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:16.230
<b>Hokuo</b>

00:04:15.130 --> 00:04:16.230
Mashima...

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:20.240
There's no point in this
 if you lose before facing me.

00:04:20.690 --> 00:04:23.450
Don't underestimate the East Japan Qualifiers.

00:04:27.290 --> 00:04:28.230
Makoto.

00:04:28.610 --> 00:04:30.650
Why are you here?
 You have exams to study for.

00:04:30.650 --> 00:04:34.120
Well, Rion, Cheers, and Eromu 
are all playing...

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:37.160
Emuro-kun, you have exams, too. 
Why are you here?

00:04:38.070 --> 00:04:40.160
Please don't ask questions 
you know the answer to.

00:04:40.630 --> 00:04:45.380
<i>I want to see Coach Sakurazawa in 
the Queen qualifiers up close.</i>

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:47.510
<i>Both her karuta and her boobs
are still going strong!</i>

00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:51.880
Mommy! Mommy!

00:04:51.010 --> 00:04:53.940
Aki! Mommy's feeding Jin right now!

00:04:51.880 --> 00:04:53.940
Wake up, Mommy!

00:04:54.280 --> 00:04:56.150
But she's asleep!

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:00.560
Jin, are you full now?

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:05.080
I'll go and win. See you next at lunch.

00:05:06.580 --> 00:05:09.650
What? Ayase-san missed this 
for her class trip?!

00:05:09.650 --> 00:05:12.020
But Mizusawa's club president is here?!

00:05:15.990 --> 00:05:18.450
So this is the Karuta Memorial Hall...

00:05:18.450 --> 00:05:20.840
You want to watch from outside? Why?

00:05:20.840 --> 00:05:24.510
Well, because it's already 
full of participants...

00:05:25.890 --> 00:05:27.460
T-Taichi?!

00:05:28.060 --> 00:05:30.740
<i>I was wondering which library he was going to...</i>

00:05:33.090 --> 00:05:35.110
<i>Taichi!</i>

00:05:36.530 --> 00:05:40.340
We will now draw the match-ups 
for the East Japan Qualifiers.

00:05:42.690 --> 00:05:45.940
Master/Queen 
West Japan Qualifiers

00:05:42.690 --> 00:05:45.940
Omi Jingu 
Learning Center

00:05:42.990 --> 00:05:45.960
I wonder how the qualifiers are 
going to play out this year.

00:05:45.960 --> 00:05:49.650
The young players, both male and female,
have been making waves lately.

00:05:49.650 --> 00:05:53.310
We need the Nagumo Society's Murao-kun
to complete his comeback, don't we?

00:05:53.310 --> 00:05:57.220
Nah, as long as someone brings down 
the current Master, I don't care who wins.

00:05:59.180 --> 00:06:03.090
Personally, I think it'll 
be Wataya Arata-kun.

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:03.090
All Japan Senior High School Cultural Federation 
Karuta Division 
Yoshioka Hirokazu

00:06:04.600 --> 00:06:07.700
That goes without saying, Mr. Yoshioka.

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:11.670
The traces of Master Wataya are 
increasingly visible in him.

00:06:13.340 --> 00:06:16.680
Master Wataya was fond of the Monk Saigyo.

00:06:16.680 --> 00:06:18.470
He had an intellectual side.

00:06:18.470 --> 00:06:22.940
And his strength when he and Sato Kiyohiko 
were competing as the top two...

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:25.310
He wasn't just fast.

00:06:25.310 --> 00:06:27.980
He had grace and power, too.

00:06:28.910 --> 00:06:32.950
I'm sure he'll live up to our expectations.

00:06:35.370 --> 00:06:37.080
What's wrong, Arata?

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:39.070
N-Nothing.

00:06:40.280 --> 00:06:41.820
<i>I know what did it.</i>

00:06:41.830 --> 00:06:43.960
<b>Mom sent this</b>

00:06:42.470 --> 00:06:47.570
<i>It was the huge plate of katsuo sandwiches 
with katsuobushi that Yuu made this morning.</i>

00:06:48.120 --> 00:06:51.080
<i>Damn, I ate too much of something 
I shouldn't have eaten at all.</i>

00:06:51.970 --> 00:06:53.500
<i>Gotta get to the bathroom...</i>

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:00.810
<i>Mashima Taichi</i>

00:07:01.810 --> 00:07:03.050
<i>Taichi?!</i>

00:07:03.350 --> 00:07:06.720
We're going to Kyoto for our class trip!

00:07:06.720 --> 00:07:09.630
<i>Chihaya said they had their class trip!</i>

00:07:10.620 --> 00:07:12.320
<i>Does this mean...</i>

00:07:13.610 --> 00:07:16.580
<i>Taichi's serious about trying 
to become the Master?</i>

00:07:16.580 --> 00:07:19.370
It was mostly Chihaya being so pushy.

00:07:19.600 --> 00:07:22.130
<i>I didn't think he was that serious.</i>

00:07:22.130 --> 00:07:26.290
<i>I thought he was just playing 
because Chihaya was.</i>

00:07:29.200 --> 00:07:32.430
Hey! You need to turn off 
your engine! Quickly!

00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:38.250
Chairman Mashita, you sure like 
helping people out, don't you?

00:07:38.250 --> 00:07:39.130
Shinobu-chan?

00:07:39.130 --> 00:07:43.660
You gave him not only my phone number,
 but my address, too?

00:07:43.660 --> 00:07:45.020
I-I'm sorry...

00:07:45.020 --> 00:07:48.320
It was a heck of a shock when 
he showed up at my house!

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:52.030
<b>Sorry!</b>

00:07:48.320 --> 00:07:52.150
Knowing you, I figured you'd just 
send him packing anyway...

00:07:52.510 --> 00:07:57.120
But I guess even you couldn't resist 
being swept up in the Master's pace.

00:08:01.840 --> 00:08:03.530
<i>Master Suo?!</i>

00:08:04.410 --> 00:08:07.200
Oh, what a funny joke.

00:08:07.200 --> 00:08:08.680
I liked the side—

00:08:08.680 --> 00:08:10.170
Never mind.

00:08:10.170 --> 00:08:11.620
<i>She wanted to ride in the side car.</i>

00:08:11.620 --> 00:08:12.830
<i>She wanted to try the side car.</i>

00:08:12.830 --> 00:08:13.880
<i>In the side car...</i>

00:08:13.880 --> 00:08:14.680
<i>Side car...</i>

00:08:15.900 --> 00:08:17.430
<i>Still...</i>

00:08:17.820 --> 00:08:21.560
<i>What are the Master and Queen doing 
at the West Japan qualifiers?</i>

00:08:23.700 --> 00:08:24.550
Here.

00:08:25.650 --> 00:08:28.190
Are you in Class A?

00:08:28.190 --> 00:08:29.260
Uh, yes...

00:08:29.260 --> 00:08:29.980
Then here.

00:08:30.370 --> 00:08:31.070
And you?

00:08:31.070 --> 00:08:32.140
I-I'm Class A...

00:08:32.140 --> 00:08:34.940
<i>Master Suo's handing out sweets again!</i>

00:08:33.070 --> 00:08:33.910
Here.

00:08:34.170 --> 00:08:34.960
Here.

00:08:34.960 --> 00:08:37.410
<i>So that's Suo Hisashi...</i>

00:08:37.410 --> 00:08:40.910
<i>I've seen him on TV several times,
but this is the first time in person.</i>

00:08:41.460 --> 00:08:42.460
<i>I remember...</i>

00:08:42.460 --> 00:08:46.810
<i>When Suo-san first became the Master, 
I was watching with Grandpa.</i>

00:08:47.360 --> 00:08:50.630
Hey, Grandpa, what's the Master match like?

00:08:50.630 --> 00:08:52.450
Do even you get nervous?

00:08:52.450 --> 00:08:54.130
Not at all.

00:08:54.130 --> 00:08:58.300
The new Master is college student Suo Hisashi.

00:08:58.710 --> 00:09:02.900
I heard he only started 
playing karuta in college.

00:09:02.900 --> 00:09:06.370
I guess there are geniuses with 
amazing game sense out there.

00:09:10.240 --> 00:09:13.900
<i>"When you eventually challenge for the throne,</i>

00:09:15.560 --> 00:09:17.660
<i>you'll probably be facing that new Master."</i>

00:09:19.140 --> 00:09:22.140
Suo-kun, what brings you here?

00:09:22.140 --> 00:09:24.880
Chairman, would you like a dorayaki?

00:09:24.880 --> 00:09:27.820
What? Sorry, you'll have to speak up!

00:09:27.820 --> 00:09:30.430
Chairman, would you like a dorayaki?

00:09:30.430 --> 00:09:32.920
Speak up! My hearing's 
not so good, you know!

00:09:34.420 --> 00:09:40.950
I said in that interview that there 
are 28 one-syllable cards for me,

00:09:40.950 --> 00:09:44.420
but I counted again recently, 
and there were 27.

00:09:43.520 --> 00:09:46.190
<b>Get a hold of yourself!</b>

00:09:44.420 --> 00:09:46.310
What? 27?

00:09:46.310 --> 00:09:50.410
I think I'll finally be able to earn the credit
 for the German class I kept failing,

00:09:50.410 --> 00:09:52.310
so I should finally graduate this year.

00:09:52.310 --> 00:09:56.060
That's great! Well done! Congrats! 
Do you have a job lined up?

00:09:56.480 --> 00:10:00.020
The place where I've been working 
part-time said they'd hire me.

00:09:59.030 --> 00:10:01.330
<b>Oh, yeah?</b>

00:10:00.020 --> 00:10:01.330
So...

00:10:02.590 --> 00:10:05.820
After I win my fifth consecutive title,
 I'm going to retire.

00:10:08.980 --> 00:10:09.740
<i>What?</i>

00:10:10.520 --> 00:10:13.620
<i>The Master... is retiring?</i>

00:10:14.890 --> 00:10:17.710
Hallelujah!

00:10:17.710 --> 00:10:19.920
<i>After his fifth consecutive win?</i>

00:10:23.350 --> 00:10:23.850
<b>Fine Confections 
Kogetsuan</b>

00:10:23.850 --> 00:10:24.850
<b>Clench</b>

00:10:23.850 --> 00:10:24.850
Kyoko-tan!

00:10:25.460 --> 00:10:29.910
Kyoko-tan is the reader for
 the West Japan qualifiers this year!

00:10:30.710 --> 00:10:33.890
It must be fate!

00:10:34.200 --> 00:10:36.350
I guess he <i>can</i> speak loudly.

00:10:37.040 --> 00:10:39.200
<i>Despite how noisy and crowded this place is,</i>

00:10:39.200 --> 00:10:42.060
<i>he still picked up her voice
from that far away.</i>

00:10:42.060 --> 00:10:43.880
<i>And he's talking about retiring?</i>

00:10:45.920 --> 00:10:47.360
<i>Is he mocking us?!</i>

00:10:47.360 --> 00:10:48.990
<i>Cocky bastard!</i>

00:10:48.990 --> 00:10:50.940
<i>Talking like a five-peat is guaranteed!</i>

00:10:50.940 --> 00:10:52.870
<i>I won't let him quit while he's ahead!</i>

00:11:20.460 --> 00:11:23.690
<i>That I'd become the Master 
was my promise to Grandpa.</i>

00:11:26.320 --> 00:11:30.330
<i>It has nothing to do with my dream.</i>

00:11:32.170 --> 00:11:33.220
<i>Let's do this.</i>

00:11:41.560 --> 00:11:44.080
Shinobu-chan, is he your friend?

00:11:45.120 --> 00:11:47.720
Just a river in my way.

00:11:56.700 --> 00:11:59.690
<i>No one in his age group is 
a match for him anymore.</i>

00:12:05.660 --> 00:12:08.290
<b>Why'd he send a card?</b>

00:12:06.040 --> 00:12:08.290
<i>Arata got that one!</i>

00:12:13.910 --> 00:12:15.620
<i>He never argues.</i>

00:12:15.960 --> 00:12:19.420
<i>And that posture came 
straight from Master Wataya.</i>

00:12:21.910 --> 00:12:25.260
I can tell you're not 
envisioning your own victory.

00:12:26.290 --> 00:12:27.500
<i>Envision...</i>

00:12:29.020 --> 00:12:30.330
<i>Envision...</i>

00:12:31.550 --> 00:12:33.010
<i>Envision my victory...</i>

00:12:34.690 --> 00:12:37.280
<i>His focus is refreshing.</i>

00:12:37.560 --> 00:12:39.850
<i>No wonder we expect so much of him...</i>

00:12:41.420 --> 00:12:47.190
<i>when we can see Master Wataya 
in that young, slender body.</i>

00:12:52.480 --> 00:12:54.130
<i>It's noon already...</i>

00:12:54.680 --> 00:12:56.780
<i>I wonder how the East qualifier's going.</i>

00:12:58.450 --> 00:13:00.050
<i>How's Taichi doing?</i>

00:13:01.340 --> 00:13:03.130
<b>Eek!</b>

00:13:03.540 --> 00:13:05.900
Er... S-Suo-san?

00:13:05.900 --> 00:13:08.400
Hello. I watched your match.

00:13:08.400 --> 00:13:11.150
<i>He's as quiet as the rumors say...</i>

00:13:11.150 --> 00:13:13.400
You're very good.

00:13:13.400 --> 00:13:15.750
Huh? N-No, I'm not...

00:13:15.750 --> 00:13:18.360
You'll be the Master one day.

00:13:18.360 --> 00:13:20.400
The Master? No, I really...

00:13:21.180 --> 00:13:23.910
But you won't be the next Master.

00:13:27.910 --> 00:13:31.590
Watching you doesn't excite me.

00:13:35.760 --> 00:13:36.990
Bye-bye.

00:13:39.270 --> 00:13:42.040
Chi-chan, where are you?!

00:13:42.040 --> 00:13:45.880
<i>Meanwhile, the main character was 
lost on the Golden Pavilion grounds.</i>

00:13:47.250 --> 00:13:49.060
Thank you for the game.

00:13:51.260 --> 00:13:55.020
<b>You're so great!</b>

00:13:52.540 --> 00:13:55.790
<i>M-Mashima and Gotokuji Saneatsu?!</i>

00:13:55.310 --> 00:14:00.520
Skreeee

00:13:56.590 --> 00:14:00.510
<i>I want both of them to lose, 
but one of them has to win!</i>

00:14:05.890 --> 00:14:07.460
<i>What am I doing?</i>

00:14:08.910 --> 00:14:10.530
<i>I wonder if everyone here</i>

00:14:11.770 --> 00:14:13.640
<i>wants to be the Master.</i>

00:14:15.780 --> 00:14:18.800
<i>I'm gonna do this! I'm gonna do this!</i>

00:14:18.790 --> 00:14:20.420
<b>Darling's on the attack!</b>

00:14:18.800 --> 00:14:20.410
<i>Mashima...</i>

00:14:23.380 --> 00:14:27.450
<i>What is it I want to become so badly</i>

00:14:28.160 --> 00:14:30.130
<i>that I'd miss my class trip?</i>

00:14:30.460 --> 00:14:32.940
<i>Taichi!</i>

00:14:33.630 --> 00:14:37.150
<i>The Master and Queen qualifiers? What?!</i>

00:14:37.460 --> 00:14:40.930
<i>I didn't know you had a stupid goal
 like wanting to be the Master of karuta!</i>

00:14:40.930 --> 00:14:42.420
<i>I don't believe it!</i>

00:14:42.420 --> 00:14:44.430
My son has a fever.

00:14:45.170 --> 00:14:47.850
<i>You even made your mother tell a lie!</i>

00:14:50.170 --> 00:14:52.140
<i>She said "Taichi."</i>

00:14:52.140 --> 00:14:54.790
<i>Is she Mashima-senpai's mother?</i>

00:14:55.450 --> 00:14:56.590
You there.

00:14:56.590 --> 00:14:57.320
Huh?

00:14:57.320 --> 00:14:59.750
What time will this match end?

00:14:59.750 --> 00:15:01.930
In about an hour...

00:15:01.930 --> 00:15:03.080
An hour?!

00:15:03.420 --> 00:15:05.580
I can't wait around here for an hour!

00:15:04.220 --> 00:15:07.580
Um, please quiet down. 
There's a match going on.

00:15:08.420 --> 00:15:12.870
Actually, we're members of 
Mashima-senpai's club.

00:15:12.870 --> 00:15:13.600
What?

00:15:13.930 --> 00:15:16.000
You two are in the karuta club?

00:15:16.000 --> 00:15:19.650
Y-Yes! We'll be here 
watching the entire time,

00:15:19.650 --> 00:15:22.530
so maybe we could contact you 
when it's about to end?

00:15:22.530 --> 00:15:23.590
Huh?

00:15:24.710 --> 00:15:26.270
Good idea.

00:15:26.700 --> 00:15:29.100
I'm going to get some tea. I appreciate it.

00:15:31.750 --> 00:15:34.670
<i>Nishida-senpai did say...</i>

00:15:35.270 --> 00:15:41.040
<i>that Mashima-senpai had a scary mom who'd 
make him quit the club if his grades dropped.</i>

00:15:41.590 --> 00:15:42.720
Tsukuba...

00:15:43.180 --> 00:15:45.630
I think this is my chance.

00:15:45.630 --> 00:15:46.630
Huh?

00:15:46.630 --> 00:15:49.820
If you want to bring down the general,
shoot his horse first.

00:15:50.370 --> 00:15:51.480
Was that the saying?

00:15:52.910 --> 00:15:55.290
This is my chance to get 
his mother to like me!

00:15:53.640 --> 00:15:59.390
<b>Huh?</b>

00:15:55.290 --> 00:15:57.890
A shortcut to my true goal!

00:16:00.100 --> 00:16:02.520
<i>My name is Hyuga Yoshihiko.</i>

00:16:02.520 --> 00:16:04.950
<i>I give my all every day 
to make girls like me.</i>

00:16:04.900 --> 00:16:08.320
Nice!

00:16:04.900 --> 00:16:08.320
You cut 
your hair?

00:16:04.950 --> 00:16:07.910
<i>My observant eye notices when a girl has 
cut her bangs one centimeter shorter!</i>

00:16:07.910 --> 00:16:10.580
<i>If the blackboard is dirty, 
that's my chance!</i>

00:16:08.320 --> 00:16:12.570
Creepy...

00:16:10.580 --> 00:16:12.560
<i>I'm diligent enough to 
volunteer for hard work!</i>

00:16:12.860 --> 00:16:14.420
<i>All this potential!</i>

00:16:14.420 --> 00:16:17.710
<i>At Fujisaki, being good at karuta
makes you attractive!</i>

00:16:17.830 --> 00:16:19.700
<b>(Note) It doesn't work on bears</b>

00:16:20.890 --> 00:16:24.070
<i>I will defeat the jerk who defeated Rion!</i>

00:16:26.040 --> 00:16:29.130
<i>My students are getting nowhere this year.</i>

00:16:26.250 --> 00:16:31.720
Won

00:16:26.630 --> 00:16:31.720
Lost in the first round

00:16:29.130 --> 00:16:30.380
<i>Why did they even come here?</i>

00:16:31.720 --> 00:16:35.970
Won

00:16:32.150 --> 00:16:34.860
<i>Inokuma-san won, unsurprisingly.</i>

00:16:34.860 --> 00:16:35.960
<i>What about Rion?</i>

00:16:38.450 --> 00:16:40.350
Rion, how'd it go?

00:16:41.550 --> 00:16:43.690
I... I won.

00:16:52.230 --> 00:16:54.980
<i>Mashima-senpai's match 
will be over soon, too.</i>

00:16:54.980 --> 00:16:57.000
<i>Time to send that message.</i>

00:16:57.310 --> 00:17:00.360
<i>It's crucial that I get 
his mother to like me!</i>

00:17:01.120 --> 00:17:05.000
<b>Mashima-senpai's Mother</b>

00:17:01.370 --> 00:17:05.010
<i>Even Mashima-senpai can't spend 
his whole life playing karuta.</i>

00:17:06.830 --> 00:17:07.500
I'm sorr—

00:17:31.810 --> 00:17:34.780
Win for Mashima, by eleven cards.

00:17:34.780 --> 00:17:36.460
<i>Mashima-senpai?</i>

00:17:36.460 --> 00:17:38.280
Y-You won, Mashima?

00:17:38.280 --> 00:17:41.880
Of course you did! That old dude's
 just been getting by on beginner's luck!

00:17:41.880 --> 00:17:43.620
It's weird that <i>I</i> lost to him!

00:17:43.620 --> 00:17:45.020
That's for sure.

00:17:45.710 --> 00:17:49.080
Why did I lose to that kid?

00:17:46.200 --> 00:17:49.380
Every card you send him, 
he sends right back.

00:17:49.380 --> 00:17:52.230
It's clear he's only 
thinking about himself.

00:17:52.230 --> 00:17:54.460
You can tell which cards 
he's going for, too.

00:17:55.110 --> 00:17:56.840
I know you're better than that!

00:17:57.930 --> 00:18:00.580
Don't lose to someone like that!

00:18:10.300 --> 00:18:12.530
<i>Why did I have to say all that?</i>

00:18:14.760 --> 00:18:16.330
<i>The next match...</i>

00:18:17.290 --> 00:18:20.070
<i>Hurry up and start the next match.</i>

00:18:27.350 --> 00:18:28.790
<i>You're wrong.</i>

00:18:29.730 --> 00:18:31.160
<i>You're wrong.</i>

00:18:31.900 --> 00:18:34.490
<i>I lost because I'm not a good player.</i>

00:18:36.660 --> 00:18:41.620
<i>Because I can't admit that 
I'm just not that good.</i>

00:18:48.660 --> 00:18:51.390
They've started. Are you sure...

00:18:51.770 --> 00:18:54.600
you don't need to contact Senpai's mom?

00:19:03.150 --> 00:19:05.710
Hey, you! What's going on?

00:19:05.710 --> 00:19:07.860
You didn't contact me, so I came to see—

00:19:16.000 --> 00:19:17.100
Move.

00:19:17.100 --> 00:19:18.550
I-I won't!

00:19:18.550 --> 00:19:19.370
Huh?

00:19:19.370 --> 00:19:20.560
I won't move!

00:19:21.990 --> 00:19:26.420
You know that karuta and this "Master"
nonsense won't get him anywhere in life!

00:19:26.770 --> 00:19:29.190
He's so stuck on a silly game
he can only play for so long!

00:19:31.700 --> 00:19:34.560
But he might play for the rest of his life!

00:19:35.210 --> 00:19:37.790
Win for Mashima, by six cards.

00:19:37.790 --> 00:19:38.960
Senpai...

00:19:39.810 --> 00:19:42.830
U-Um, you shouldn't go outside right now.

00:19:48.850 --> 00:19:50.340
Mashima-senpai...

00:19:51.290 --> 00:19:52.720
Senpai...

00:19:53.830 --> 00:19:55.290
We're getting three wins, guys.

00:19:55.290 --> 00:19:56.770
<i>Impassionate gods</i>

00:19:56.770 --> 00:19:58.180
It's about taking 10 cards 
from your opponent.

00:19:58.180 --> 00:19:59.850
And keeping 15 of your own!

00:20:00.590 --> 00:20:01.950
I'm here to practice.

00:20:02.430 --> 00:20:03.970
Thank you for the game.

00:20:06.390 --> 00:20:09.140
He's working hard to be 
what he wants to be!

00:20:12.960 --> 00:20:14.980
Wh-What are you saying?

00:20:14.980 --> 00:20:17.820
You're making no sense!

00:20:18.110 --> 00:20:20.240
<b>What are <i>you</i> saying in the 
Mecca of karuta?</b>

00:20:18.110 --> 00:20:20.240
<b>Is this lady looking for a fight?</b>

00:20:33.950 --> 00:20:36.330
We will now draw the match-ups for round 3.

00:20:37.460 --> 00:20:39.460
<b>Mizusawa</b>

00:20:39.910 --> 00:20:41.590
Who's looking good this year?

00:20:41.590 --> 00:20:43.270
Sudo-kun from Hokuo is playing well.

00:20:43.270 --> 00:20:44.390
He's improved.

00:20:44.390 --> 00:20:46.650
What about Tamaru-kun?
I had high hopes for him.

00:20:46.650 --> 00:20:48.550
Tsuboguchi-san's been winning, too.

00:20:48.830 --> 00:20:53.800
But the one who's improved the most 
has to be Koishikawa-kun of KU.

00:20:53.940 --> 00:20:56.310
Koishikawa Shusaku

00:20:54.240 --> 00:20:56.860
Whoever's matched up with 
him is out of luck.

00:20:56.310 --> 00:20:58.820
Koishikawa Shusaku

00:20:58.820 --> 00:21:00.820
<b>Mizusawa</b>

00:21:03.020 --> 00:21:06.900
Mashima, you're a coward.

00:21:10.530 --> 00:21:12.570
<i>I want to be someone who isn't me.</i>

00:21:16.940 --> 00:21:17.910
<i>But...</i>

00:21:19.120 --> 00:21:20.820
<i>I still want to be me.</i>
